@title Data subject access requests
@subtitle Runbook for handling a DSAR at Quillfeather Software
@author Privacy Officer, Owner

kpi Legal deadline | 30 days | from a valid request
kpi Internal target | Day 25 | deliver by
kpi Privacy Officer | Anneliese Vogt | privacy@quillfeather.example
kpi Escalation | #privacy-requests | channel

# Deadlines
- We must respond within **30 days** of receiving a valid request.
- Complex requests can be extended by up to **60 more days**, but only if we tell the requester within the first 30 days.
- Our internal target is to deliver by **day 25**.

# Handling steps
1. Log the request in the privacy tracker within 1 business day.
2. Verify identity within 5 business days.
-- 1. Ask for two documents.
-- 2. Never accept a photo of a card showing a full number.
3. Confirm the scope with the requester by email.
4. Collect data from the six systems listed below.
5. Legal reviews the export and redacts other people's data.
6. Package the export.
-- 1. Put it in an encrypted ZIP.
-- 2. Send the password by SMS, never in the same email.
7. Deliver by day 25 and record the delivery date.
8. Close the ticket and keep the log for 3 years.

# Systems to search
data systems = system,owner,days needed; CRM,Sales Ops,3; Billing,Finance Systems,4; Support desk,Support Ops,3; Product database,Data Platform,6; Marketing email,Growth,2; Analytics events,Data Platform,6
table systems sort=-days needed bar=days needed
! Backups are not searched, but note the date of the last backup.

# Do not
!! Do not delete data in response to an access request.
!! Do not send the export to an address that was not verified.
!! Do not discuss the request in public channels.

# Contacts
table = role,name,contact; Privacy Officer,Anneliese Vogt,privacy@quillfeather.example; Legal reviewer,Marcus Teo,; Escalation,,#privacy-requests
